Revision history for Geo-Location-Predicate

0.01	Sun Oct 18 2026
	First release: the location rule moved out of Geo-Coder-Free 0.48.

	Geo::Location::Predicate has been a module of Geo-Coder-Free since the rule
	was given one home there; it is a distribution of its own now, so that the
	six geocoders that ask it - Geo::Coder::CA, DataScienceToolkit, GeoApify,
	List, Postcodes and XYZ - can depend on one predicate instead of on the whole
	facade, its backends, its databases and its cache.  The module name, the sub
	and its answers are unchanged: what moved is which distribution ships the
	file.  Geo::Coder::Free depends on this distribution from 0.48, and the six
	declare it under recommends in their META - a recommendation for runtime, with
	a test requirement, because their suites assert its answer - and look for it
	when they first need it, refusing a reference when it is not installed.

	The repository carries the gate on the rule itself now:
	.github/workflows/location-predicates.yml assembles Geo-Coder-Free's harness and
	the six geocoders, and runs the fuzz against the rule in the branch on a push
	here and on a pull request, so a change to the rule that disagrees with the six
	fails before the merge.  The daily run in Geo-Coder-Free cannot see such a
	change: a workflow only runs in the repository its event happened in.  The
	harness is what makes the branch the tree under test - it puts the checkouts'
	lib/ ahead of everything on @INC and refuses to run when the file that loaded is
	not this distribution's.
